    "audit_note": "{\"reason\": \"Named oligonucleotide PROTACs MP-16/MP-17 inhibited tumors and exhibited promising drug safety in mice; weak safety detail so Grade C.\", \"grounding_quote\": \"Herein, by conjugating VH032 with an optimized DNA sequence that recognized c-Myc complex, we discovered oligonucleotide-based proteolysis targeting chimeras (PROTACs), termed as MP-16 and MP-17, which effectively induced degradation of c-Myc. Mechanically, MP-16 or MP-17 directly interacted with c-Myc complex to form VHL/PROTAC/c-Myc ternary complex, and triggered c-Myc degradation by recruiting ubiquitin-proteasome system, suppressing cell proliferation of HCC cells. In mice model, MP-16 or MP-17 significantly inhibited HCC tumor growth and exhibited promising drug safety.\", \"source_pmid\": \"39447458\", \"candidate_domain\": \"toxicity\"}",
