    "audit_note": "{\"reason\": \"IONIS-TTRRx ASO was administered in healthy volunteers and reported well tolerated without remarkable safety issues; abstract-only support so Grade B.\", \"grounding_quote\": \"IONIS-TTRRx (ISIS 420915) is a 2nd-Generation 2'-O-(2-methoxyethyl) modified \\\"2'-MOE\\\" antisense oligonucleotide (ASO) that targets the TTR RNA transcript and reduces the levels of the TTR transcript through an RNaseH1 mechanism of action, leading to reductions in both mutant and wild-type TTR protein. The activity of IONIS-TTRRx to decrease TTR protein levels was studied in transgenic mice bearing the Ile84Ser human TTR mutant, in cynomolgus monkeys and in healthy human volunteers. Robust (>80%) reductions of plasma TTR protein were obtained in all three species treated with IONIS-TTRRx, which in mice and monkeys was associated with substantial reductions in hepatic TTR RNA levels. These effects were dose-dependent and lasted for weeks post-dosing. In a Phase 1 healthy volunteer study, treatment with IONIS-TTRRx for four weeks was well tolerated without any remarkable safety issues.\", \"source_pmid\": \"27355239\", \"candidate_domain\": \"toxicity\"}",
    "audited_at": "2026-06-07T23:20:28.232879+00:00"
