    "audit_note": "{\"reason\": \"CManDA/DNCA/CLD lipid system delivered siG12S with tumor targeting and silencing; abstract support so Grade C.\", \"grounding_quote\": \"Here, we designed and synthesized a Gemini-type mannosylated peptidyl lipid called CManDA(M), which, in combination with the cytidinyl lipid DNCA(D) and the peptidyl lipid CLD(C) (D/50C/50M), could transfect siRNA (siG12S) into A549 cells to target and silence the KRASG12S gene. The fluorescence intensity in the tumor area of the D/50C/50M/Cy5.5-siG12S group increased by approximately 2.5 times. Furthermore, full 2'-F/2'-OMe-modified siG12Ss could also be transfected by D/50C/50M into cells, resulting in target gene silencing. The tumor weight in the D/50C/50M/M3 group (1.5 mg/kg, i.v.) was reduced by 50 % after administration in a mouse axillary tumor (A549) model, whereas the tumor bioluminescence intensity was only approximately 30 % of that in the blank group in a mouse orthotopic lung cancer model and showed no significant toxicity.\", \"source_pmid\": \"40073943\", \"candidate_domain\": \"delivery\"}",
